        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-17T17:55:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe the MKBP wake-up masks are only used on ARM based Chromebooks.\n\nFor x86 based chromebooks the wakeup mask is controlled by the AP firmware.\n\nMy suggested rewording:\n\nThe EC can wake up up the AP from sleep modes based on multiple event types. A wake-up mask specifies which specific event types are able to wake the AP.  \n\nFor x86 based Chromebooks, the wake-up mask is controlled by the AP firmware directly using host commands EC_CMD_HOST_EVENT_SET_SMI_MASK, EC_CMD_HOST_EVENT_SET_SCI_MASK, and EC_CMD_HOST_EVENT_SET_WAKE_MASK.\n\nFor ARM based Chromebooks, the wake-up mask is defined as device tree nodes, one for MKBP events and one for generic host events. They have respective Kconfig options, which must be enabled to take the\nmasks into account.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 153,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 159,
        "endChar": 0
      },
